<title>UK: Manchester Utd in TV talks - paper.</title>
<headline>Manchester Utd in TV talks - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>British football club Manchester United Plc is holding talks with three companies on launching a television channel, a British newspaper reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Talks are at an early stage and the club has not yet decided whether it would run the programmes or sell the rights, the Daily Telegraph said, quoting chief executive Martin Edwards.</p>
<p>The newspaper did not identify the companies said to be involved in the discussions with the club.</p>
<p>United on Monday announced an increase in pre-tax profit for the six months to end-January to 19.45 million pounds ($31.8 million) from 15.28 million.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44-171-542-7717</p>
<p>($ = 0.611 British Pounds)</p>
